{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73op8ZUh6f11kHic957","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Install uv first if you don't have it:\n\n```bash\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh   # macOS/Linux\n# or: pip install uv / brew install uv\n```\n\nThen create a project:\n\n```bash\nuv init my-project      # creates a new directory\ncd my-project\n```\n\nOr, to initialize in an existing directory, run `uv init` with no name.\n\n`uv init` creates:\n- `pyproject.toml`\n- `main.py`\n- `README.md`\n- `.python-version`\n- a git repo (when git is available)\n\n**Common next steps**\n\n```bash\nuv add requests            # add a dependency (creates .venv and uv.lock)\nuv add --dev pytest        # add a dev dependency\nuv run main.py             # run a script in the project's environment\nuv run pytest              # run any command in the environment\nuv sync                    # install everything from the lockfile\nuv python pin 3.12         # pin a Python version\n```\n\n**Useful variants**\n- `uv init --lib my-lib` creates a library with a `src/` layout.\n- `uv init --package my-app` creates a packaged app with a `src/` layout and a CLI entry point.\n- `uv init --python 3.12` sets the Python version.\n\nYou don't need to activate the virtualenv, because `uv run` uses `.venv` automatically. To activate it manually, run `source .venv/bin/activate`.\n\nI can run these in your working directory if you'd like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6835,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6835},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f1751e4-b639-4944-b0b6-1319a1cd2cf8"